# Agent Guidelines for Crop Yield Prediction Project

- Notebook-First Research Workflow: Core research, EDA, outlier handling, feature engineering, feature selection experiments, model training, and evaluations must reside in `notebooks/` (`01_*.ipynb` through `09_*.ipynb`).
- Keep reusable utilities in `src/` (`src/data`, `src/preprocessing`, `src/features`, `src/models`, `src/evaluation`) and import them into notebooks.
- NEVER modify or overwrite `data/raw/crop_yield_dataset.csv`.
- Adhere strictly to the phased development strategy. Implement ONLY the requested phase.
- Ensure every feature selector adheres to the `fit(X, y)` and `transform(X)` contract.
- Never fit feature selectors or scalers using validation or test datasets.
- Test set (2015–2017) must remain completely untouched until final benchmark reporting.
- Propose conventional commit messages and ask for user approval before committing or pushing changes to Git.
